From 5cefa76625ebe5da34ad510f63756087c831562a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RaikaShinohara <321751277+RaikaShinohara@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 16:59:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: wire Galaxy Book4 Edge Type-C ports

Connect each S2MM006 PD controller to its dual-role DWC3 controller,
PS8830 retimer and PTN3222 eUSB2 repeater. Use the board's actual
sideband signal path and PHY supplies. The USB-A controller keeps
its original wiring.

Both Type-C ports bound to EmuEC on the test boot. USB storage
re-enumerated after hotplug on the rear port.

Source: https://github.com/anatase-org/patchwork/tree/5fcc40d7a4bfc7ac91fc080c384b71331e23def7
---
